{
  "verdict": "needs_update",
  "status": "introduced",
  "candidates": [
    {
      "candidate_id": "c1",
      "source_id": "notes_uninitialized",
      "origin": "review-1",
      "kind": "lifecycle",
      "change_ids": [
        "g0006",
        "g0007"
      ],
      "requirement": "Initialize the notes obstack before the assembly pass creates sections.",
      "target_route": "LLVMFuzzerTestOneInput calls read_begin, then perform_an_assembly_pass(2, fakeArgv). The pass calls subseg_new; subseg_get allocates section information from notes when that information is absent.",
      "failure_condition": "For a newly created section without segment information, alloc_seginfo uses obstack_alloc on notes, while the entry has bypassed its initialization in main.",
      "alternative_paths": "The complete entry never calls main or another notes initializer. read_begin initializes cond_obstack, not notes. The section creation precedes reading the fuzzer's file, so changing its bytes cannot avoid this route.",
      "discovery_necessary": true,
      "discovery_established": true
    }
  ],
  "decisions": [
    {
      "candidate_id": "c1",
      "decision": "keep",
      "errors": [],
      "obligation_class": "execution_compatibility",
      "citation_errors": []
    }
  ],
  "scope_complete": false,
  "timing": {
    "status": "introduced",
    "gap": true,
    "introduced_by_this_change": true,
    "claims": [
      {
        "claim_id": "c1",
        "status": "introduced",
        "necessary": "yes",
        "before": {
          "requirement": "Initialize notes before the assembly pass creates sections.",
          "applicability": "required",
          "harness_status": "sat",
          "reason": "The old harness calls read_begin before the assembly pass, and before-source read_begin initializes notes.",
          "source_evidence": [
            {
              "evidence_id": "loc-03734b8c6e0d98bc6c7a5c28",
              "quote": "void\nread_begin (void)\n{\n  const char *p;\n\n  pobegin ();\n  obj_read_begin_hook ();\n\n  /* Something close -- but not too close -- to a multiple of 1024.\n     The debugging malloc I'm using has 24 bytes of overhead.  */\n  obstack_begin (&notes, chunksize);\n  obstack_begin (&cond_obstack, chunksize);\n\n#ifndef tc_line_separator_chars\n#define tc_line_separator_chars line_separator_chars\n#endif\n  /* Use machine dependent syntax.  */\n  for (p = tc_line_separator_chars; *p; p++)\n    is_end_of_line[(unsigned char) *p] = 2;\n  /* Use more.  FIXME-SOMEDAY.  */\n\n  if (flag_mri)\n    lex_type['?'] = 3;\n}\n"
            },
            {
              "evidence_id": "loc-c09b9a3c778b884fa4e119b6",
              "quote": "  need_pass_2 = 0;\n\n#ifndef OBJ_MACH_O\n  /* Create the standard sections, and those the assembler uses\n     internally.  */\n  text_section = subseg_new (TEXT_SECTION_NAME, 0);\n  data_section = subseg_new (DATA_SECTION_NAME, 0);\n  bss_section = subseg_new (BSS_SECTION_NAME, 0);\n  /* @@ FIXME -- we're setting the RELOC flag so that sections are assumed\n     to have relocs, otherwise we don't find out in time.  */\n  applicable = bfd_applicable_section_flags (stdoutput);\n  bfd_set_section_flags (text_section,\n\t\t\t applicable & (SEC_ALLOC | SEC_LOAD | SEC_RELOC\n\t\t\t\t       | SEC_CODE | SEC_READONLY));\n  bfd_set_section_flags (data_section,\n\t\t\t applicable & (SEC_ALLOC | SEC_LOAD | SEC_RELOC\n\t\t\t\t       | SEC_DATA));\n  bfd_set_section_flags (bss_section, applicable & SEC_ALLOC);\n  seg_info (bss_section)->bss = 1;\n#endif\n  subseg_new (BFD_ABS_SECTION_NAME, 0);\n  subseg_new (BFD_UND_SECTION_NAME, 0);\n  reg_section = subseg_new (\"*GAS `reg' section*\", 0);\n  expr_section = subseg_new (\"*GAS `expr' section*\", 0);\n"
            }
          ]
        },
        "after": {
          "requirement": "Initialize notes before the assembly pass creates sections now that read_begin no longer does so.",
          "applicability": "required",
          "harness_status": "unsat",
          "reason": "After-source initializes notes in main, which the harness bypasses. Its call to read_begin initializes only cond_obstack before the pass creates sections.",
          "source_evidence": [
            {
              "evidence_id": "loc-bb75f5ac82c40a82dff001aa",
              "quote": "  obstack_begin (&notes, chunksize);\n  xatexit (free_notes);\n\n  PROGRESS (1);\n  /* Call parse_args before any of the init/begin functions\n     so that switches like --hash-size can be honored.  */\n  parse_args (&argc, &argv);\n"
            },
            {
              "evidence_id": "loc-429ad8ed0938cdc556d18bf4",
              "quote": "void\nread_begin (void)\n{\n  const char *p;\n\n  pobegin ();\n  obj_read_begin_hook ();\n\n  obstack_begin (&cond_obstack, chunksize);\n\n#ifndef tc_line_separator_chars\n#define tc_line_separator_chars line_separator_chars\n#endif\n  /* Use machine dependent syntax.  */\n  for (p = tc_line_separator_chars; *p; p++)\n    is_end_of_line[(unsigned char) *p] = 2;\n  /* Use more.  FIXME-SOMEDAY.  */\n\n  if (flag_mri)\n    lex_type['?'] = 3;\n}\n"
            },
            {
              "evidence_id": "loc-52814f1a6d8a0196ec799e9d",
              "quote": "  need_pass_2 = 0;\n\n#ifndef OBJ_MACH_O\n  /* Create the standard sections, and those the assembler uses\n     internally.  */\n  text_section = subseg_new (TEXT_SECTION_NAME, 0);\n  data_section = subseg_new (DATA_SECTION_NAME, 0);\n  bss_section = subseg_new (BSS_SECTION_NAME, 0);\n  /* @@ FIXME -- we're setting the RELOC flag so that sections are assumed\n     to have relocs, otherwise we don't find out in time.  */\n  applicable = bfd_applicable_section_flags (stdoutput);\n  bfd_set_section_flags (text_section,\n\t\t\t applicable & (SEC_ALLOC | SEC_LOAD | SEC_RELOC\n\t\t\t\t       | SEC_CODE | SEC_READONLY));\n  bfd_set_section_flags (data_section,\n\t\t\t applicable & (SEC_ALLOC | SEC_LOAD | SEC_RELOC\n\t\t\t\t       | SEC_DATA));\n  bfd_set_section_flags (bss_section, applicable & SEC_ALLOC);\n  seg_info (bss_section)->bss = 1;\n#endif\n  subseg_new (BFD_ABS_SECTION_NAME, 0);\n  subseg_new (BFD_UND_SECTION_NAME, 0);\n  reg_section = subseg_new (\"*GAS `reg' section*\", 0);\n  expr_section = subseg_new (\"*GAS `expr' section*\", 0);\n"
            }
          ]
        },
        "same_blocker": "no",
        "reason": "The same harness call sequence satisfied initialization before the change through read_begin. After the change, that sequence omits the initialization because its new site is main.",
